flowchart TB
    accTitle: Which PHP checks a Nextcloud app
    accDescr: Renovate keeps the tools of composer.json current, with only the releases that run on the PHP of the tools, each major version on its own and PHPUnit below 13. The CI reads two versions of PHP from the files of the app: config.platform.php of composer.json, for which Composer locks the tools, and the min-version of the PHP in appinfo/info.xml, the oldest PHP that the app runs on. It sets up the oldest PHP first and the PHP of the tools last, so that php runs the tools. php-cs-fixer, Psalm for PHP 8.2 and PHPUnit in a new random order run on the PHP of the tools; then the step Oldest PHP parses the code that the app ships with php8.2 and checks that its packages install there.

    renovate["Renovate: tools for PHP 8.3, each major<br>version on its own, PHPUnit below 13"]
    composer(["composer.json<br>config.platform.php 8.3.16"])
    info(["appinfo/info.xml<br>php min-version 8.2"])
    setup["The CI sets up PHP 8.2,<br>then PHP 8.3 for php"]
    tools["PHP 8.3: php-cs-fixer, Psalm for PHP 8.2,<br>PHPUnit 12 in random order"]
    oldest["php8.2: the syntax of what the app ships,<br>composer check-platform-reqs --no-dev"]
    app["An app that runs on PHP 8.2 and newer"]

    renovate --> composer
    composer --> setup
    info --> setup
    setup --> tools --> oldest --> app

    classDef you fill:#f59e0b2e,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px
    classDef bot fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
    classDef done fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    class composer,info you
    class renovate,setup,tools,oldest bot
